## Rework outcome

- Added `archive-assets` to `scripts/relay_release.py`. It packages only the exact canonical four-target layout using a deterministic gzip stream and USTAR records.
- The archive writer rejects extra files such as AppleDouble `._*` members and rejects source executables unless their mode is exactly `0755`.
- Every tar member is a regular file with mode `0755`, uid/gid `0`, owner/group `root`, integer mtime `1784656987`, and no PAX headers. Stable target order is `darwin-amd64`, `darwin-arm64`, `linux-amd64`, then `linux-arm64`.
- Added a regression test over the emitted tar stream. It asserts exact names/count/order/type/mode/ownership/mtime, empty PAX headers, sizes, hashes, absence/rejection of AppleDouble members, deterministic overwrite behavior, and rejection of non-`0755` source bytes.
- Recreated and updated `TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz` through `task-board resource update` from the four already-verified canonical executable bytes.

