 - VERIFICATION: Four-worker loaded harness stress, an independent clean 446-test full suite, clean 446-test coverage suite, strict recursive Swift format, core boundaries, diff check, and board validation all exited 0. Signal exit 143, empty output, zero directory/socket residue, and exactly-one managed-task cancellation remain asserted; the injected startup failure terminates with its exact diagnostic and zero retained waiters.
 - SAFETY: The delta is test-only and adds no sleep/timeout extension, retry, weaker assertion, signing, installation, launch, VPN/network preference mutation, route change, or DNS change. Commit-confirmed terminal movement remains with the orchestrator.
+
+### 0615 — Relay archive replacement uses invocation-owned temporary files (TASK-260715-24icoz)
+- REVIEW FINDING: The first deterministic archive writer opened a predictable sibling `.<archive>.tmp`, so a planted symlink could redirect writes into a victim and later become the final archive.
+- FIX: Archive creation now uses an exclusive randomized standard-library temporary file in the destination directory, cleans it only when its recorded device/inode identity still matches, atomically replaces the destination, and verifies the result is a regular non-symlink file.
+- VERIFICATION: The command-level regression preserves the planted symlink and victim across success and injected replacement failure, checks safe cleanup, and revalidates the exact four-member USTAR contract. The 35 release tests, Go tests/vet, 81.2% affected coverage, rootless native arm64/Rosetta smokes, lint, board-download archive hash/metadata, and privacy checks pass.
